-- title:
--   Unique discrete place of the Gauss sheet at a closed point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_1$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained, via `laurentBaseChange`, as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`, i.e. of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra fraction-ring model of $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$, and with $K_1$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K_1$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot$(the rational $j$-numerator power series). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$ whose elements are exactly the $f$ admitting a presentation $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $x, y$ power series over $A$ and $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, and assume $W_0$ contains the subalgebra $A_1 =$ `chartAlgFin A K₁ j` of elements of $K_1$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ whose prime ideal contains $\varpi$, contains every $s \in A_1$ lying in the nonunits of $W_0$, and contains some $s$ not lying in the nonunits of $W_0$. Writing $\rho$ for the composite $A_1 \hookrightarrow W_0 \to \kappa(W_0)$ into the residue field of $W_0$, the conclusion asserts the existence of a valuation subring $P$ of $\kappa(W_0)$ with: $\rho(s) \in P$ for all $s \in A_1$; $\rho(s)$ lies in the nonunits of $P$ if and only if $s$ lies in the prime of $y$; $P$ is the unique valuation subring of $\kappa(W_0)$ with these two properties; every $e \in P$ satisfies $e - \rho(s) \in$ nonunits of $P$ for some $s \in A_1$; and $P$ is a principal ideal ring.
--
--   This is the pointwise unibranch statement for the $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ storey of the two-chart integral model: the Gauss component carries, at each closed point $y$ of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart lying on that component and distinct from its generic point, a unique place of the residue field $\kappa(W_0)$ centred at $y$, with trivial residue extension and discrete (principal) valuation. It is used in the computations of inertia at points of the supersingular locus for the two-chart integral models of $X_1(M) \cap X_0(p)$ and of $X_0(pM)$.
